{"id":"h260","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"simpleqa","question":"What is a bridge called in the Kashmiri language? Is the answer \"Kadal\"?","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"OpenAI SimpleQA (openai/simple-evals, simple_qa_test_set.csv)","claims":[{"text":"In Kashmiri, a bridge is called kadal.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Kadal is widely used in Kashmiri and appears in many Srinagar place names such as Zaina Kadal, Fateh Kadal, Safa Kadal and Alamgiri Kadal.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"These Srinagar places are named after bridges at or near those locations.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Standard references on Kashmiri vocabulary and place names give kadal as the word for bridge.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Regional and dialectal variation means other terms might be used for bridge in some contexts.","confidence":0.3,"lean":-0.4,"theta":0.4712,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Differences in romanization, such as kadal versus kadl, mean spelling alone does not settle the matter.","confidence":0.3,"lean":-0.2,"theta":0.4712,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Kashmiri has general words for crossing or passage that might be confused with the noun for bridge.","confidence":0.25,"lean":-0.3,"theta":0.3927,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Dialect and spelling differences affect how the word is written, not what it means, so they do not outweigh the evidence for kadal.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.3,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":-0.2,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":